    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d45">

                <pb facs="0082" n="28" sameAs="frus:frus1944Quebec/pg28"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Roosevelt Papers: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">President Roosevelt to Prime Minister
                        Churchill</hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d45-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">top secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hyde
                                Park</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian" when="1944-09-01"
                            >1 September 1944</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Number 614, personal and top secret, from the President to the Prime
                    Minister.</p>
                <p>So happy your temperature is normal but this is the time to go slow. Remember I
                    am entirely free and can go to <hi rendition="#small-caps">Octagon</hi>
                    literally any time if the doctors suggest a postponement for a week or several
                    weeks. I suggest you make Clemmie<anchor n="2" xml:id="d45-f2"/> the arbiter.
                    The armies keep rolling along and a few weeks of delay on our part will not slow
                    them up.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Roosevelt</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d45-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d45-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to the White House Map Room; forwarded to the United States Naval Attaché,
                    London, via Navy channels.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d45-f2" n="2" xml:id="d45-f2-content">
                <p>Mrs. Churchill.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
